   "reply": "`python tools/check.py` now passes. The one unit test is OK and there were no line-length violations. I didn't change any code.\n\nThe script failed at first with `KeyError: 'NOTES_HOME'` because it reads that environment variable and I hadn't set it. `NOTES_HOME` is the directory where the store writes `notes.json`. To fix it, I set `NOTES_HOME` to a fresh temp directory for the run:\n\n```\nexport NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; python tools/check.py\n```\n\nThe variable has to be set again in each new shell. If you want plain `python tools/check.py` to work, `check.py` could fall back to a temp directory when the variable is unset. I haven't made that change.",
